From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:59:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08037/11362] Four of the five ARC induction failures are
 broken code, and all four are mechanically detectable

PHASE 2 asked whether the four broken-code failures the 2026-07-30 gate audit found -- ft09
and tu93 falling off the end of engine(), lp85's UnboundLocalError, ft09 round 2's truncation
-- can be caught before the trust gate sees them, and at what false-positive cost. They can,
at zero measured false positives, and the checks are proven against the failures themselves
rather than against fixtures invented to make them look good.

EACH CHECK PINNED TO ITS OWN FAILURE. ft09 is proven on the REAL live engine read off disk
(upstream_ft09_cells/on__ft09__s1__world_model.py.frozen): the static check flags it, and
executing it confirms engine(grid, 6, data) is None while the action != 6 path is fine -- a
per-path defect, exactly as the audit describes. tu93's shape falls to the same check. lp85
is caught ONLY by the goal arm of the dry run, because its UnboundLocalError comes out of
is_level_complete, not engine; an engine-only dry run reports nothing for that file, and a
test pins that near-miss. ft09 round 2 is caught by truncation detection, which must also
report NOTHING ELSE about a truncated file: it has no end, so "it never returns" would be a
false statement about it, and feeding a half-written file back as a repair spends the very
budget the retry needs.

FALSE POSITIVES, 439 REAL GENERATED ENGINES. Every world_model*.py in results/ -- banked
engines, origin fixtures, logo snapshot, every per-experiment e3_store. 9 flagged (2.05%),
9 of 9 confirmed by EXECUTING the engine and observing a real None return, 0 unconfirmed. The
worst reproduces the ft09 mode exactly: vc33's engine echoed its own refactor prompt back as
comments, including the literal REQUIRED OUTPUT STRUCTURE block, and never wrote a return.

SENSITIVITY, 36 REAL LIVE COMPLETIONS replayed from the Phase-1 capture with their recorded
stop_type: 13 that the shipped generate() ACCEPTED carry a missing_return -- broken code that
reached the trust gate as a bad prediction -- and 10 that it REJECTED are retryable
truncations, incomplete observations discarded as bad models. Cross-checked against Phase 1's
independently-written AST return check: 0 disagreements on all 28 comparable rows.

A LIVE DEFECT, NOT ONLY A HISTORICAL ONE: the banked results/arc_e3/tu93/world_model.py raises
ValueError: could not broadcast input array from shape (2,) into shape (3,) on action=4. The
trust gate can only ever see that as "failed the transition".

42 tests, 12/12 mutations killed (mutation_check.json; baseline green, module restored
byte-identical). The mutations reverse design decisions, not characters: "an if without an
else terminates" blinds the ft09/tu93 detection; "drop the goal arm" misses lp85; "the repair
prompt includes unrepairable defects" spends the budget the retry needs.

THE FUNNEL IS UNCHANGED AND THIS DOES NOT MOVE IT. Stated rather than buried. Phase 1 already
measured that under the shipped sampler EVERY ft09 engine-only attempt at 4096, 8192 and 16384
was non-returning, so even wired in, this converts "accepted a None-returning engine" into
"rejected after three tries" -- a correct diagnosis, not a working engine. Whether the REPAIR
turns a rejection into a usable engine is a live measurement not yet made. The shipped induce
path is UNCHANGED by this commit; the module is standalone.

A CLEAN REPORT IS NOT A QUALITY CLAIM, and the design refuses to let it become one. The module
has no power to admit anything and sits entirely upstream of the trust gate. Phase 1's
best-scoring completions were the identity function, which clears every check here trivially;
test_identity_engine_passes_every_check pins that, and engine_changes_anything is reported
beside a clean report so "no defects found" is never read as "the engine is good". No
threshold was lowered.

Limitation: lp85's actual source no longer exists (per-cell temp store), so the goal_raised
arm is proven against a RECONSTRUCTION of the documented mechanism and 0 preserved corpus
instances. The corpus shows it is not trigger-happy (71 engines x 50 grids, zero goal
defects), but that arm's sensitivity rests on a reconstruction, not an artefact.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6052. Banked ARC levels remain 3/3; the submission gate is NOT met.

